From 429646407ee397c4ab9008475699a7f7e165e5f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Cast: Run the media route controller on the CastV2
 session

Selecting a route now opens a CastDeviceSession to the receiver instead of
a chromecast-java-api-v2 connection. The controller reports connecting,
connected and disconnected state from the session callbacks, follows the
device volume from RECEIVER_STATUS and sets it through SET_VOLUME.

Volume changes use the route's own connection when it is up, otherwise a
session an app opened through the device controller (CastChannelRegistry),
so the slider also works while the route connection is still being set up
or failed. Callbacks of a session that was already replaced are ignored.

This removes the last user of chromecast-java-api-v2.
